# WN22-MS-000060: Windows Server 2022 must restrict remote calls to the Security Account Manager (SAM) to Administrators on domain-joined member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-ms-000060-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 must restrict remote calls to the Security Account Manager (SAM) to Administrators on domain-joined member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems.`
    description `The Windows SAM stores users' passwords. Restricting Remote Procedure Call (RPC) connections to the SAM to Administrators helps protect those credentials.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,reg-sz,medium,ksi-iam-jit`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-JIT,NIST-800-53:AC-6(10)`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-JIT`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Navigate to the policy Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Network access: Restrict clients allowed to make remote calls to SAM. Select "Edit Security" to configure the "Security descriptor:". Add "Administrators" in "Group or user names:" if it is not already listed (this is the default). Select "Administrators" in "Group or user names:". Select "Allow" for "Remote Access" in "Permissions for "Administrators". Click "OK". The `

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_KSI_IAM_JIT `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-JIT by setting registry value 'RestrictRemoteSAM' (REG_SZ) under 'HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Lsa' to the STIG-required value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match. Remediation sets the value via Group Policy or direct registry edit.`
    impl_AC_6_10 `Windows Server implements AC-6(10) by setting registry value 'RestrictRemoteSAM' (REG_SZ) under 'HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Lsa' to the STIG-required value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match. Remediation sets the value via Group Policy or direct registry edit.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Lsa`
        name `RestrictRemoteSAM`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value string = `O:BAG:BAD:(A;;RC;;;BA)`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
